---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="Accessibility" description="Accessibility goals and feedback route for the SPARK Community Hub.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Community trust" title="Accessibility is part of the product." description="The hub is being built toward WCAG 2.2 Level AA and will continue to improve as content, media, forms, and event information are added." status="preview" statusLabel="Initial statement" compact />
  <section class="section section-white"><article class="narrow prose"><h2>Current design commitments</h2><ul><li>Semantic page regions, ordered headings, and a skip link.</li><li>Keyboard-operable navigation, controls, filters, and accordions.</li><li>Visible focus indicators and status labels that do not rely on color alone.</li><li>Responsive layouts designed to reflow without horizontal page scrolling.</li><li>Readable text sizing, spacing, and contrast.</li><li>Reduced animation for visitors who request it.</li><li>Accessible HTML as the primary source for essential program information.</li></ul><h2>Media and documents</h2><p>Informative images should include meaningful alternative text. Decorative images use empty alt text. Videos selected for publication should include captions, and important recordings should include transcripts where feasible. A PDF will not be the only source for essential agenda, travel, or participation information.</p><h2>Known limitations</h2><p>This is an initial site. Automated and manual accessibility review will continue, especially after search, external forms, video, detailed schedules, downloadable documents, and richer interactive features are introduced.</p><h2>Feedback</h2><p>If something prevents you from accessing content or completing a task, email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}?subject=SPARK%20website%20accessibility`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a> with the page address, the problem, and your preferred way to receive the information. Do not include sensitive disability or health details in ordinary email.</p><p><em>Last updated: August 12, 2026.</em></p></article></section>
</BaseLayout>
